{"arrivo":"fr","origine":"gem-pro","origine_nome":"Proto-Germanic","n":15,"parole":[{"parola":"bannière","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"banner","termine_origine":"*bandiz","catena":[{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*bandiz","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*bʰendʰ-","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Inherited from Old French baniere."},{"parola":"bière","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":2,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"bier","termine_origine":"*bērō","catena":[{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*bērō","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gem-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Inherited from Old French biere, from Proto-Germanic *bērō; cognate with German Bahre and English bier."},{"parola":"bot","pos":"adj","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Unknown; perhaps","significato":"affected by the deformation known as clubfoot","termine_origine":"*buttaz","catena":[{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*buttaz","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gem-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Middle French bot (16th c.). Of unknown origin. Perhaps ultimately from Proto-Germanic *buttaz (“butt, stump, end”). If so, a doublet of but."},{"parola":"bouder","pos":"verb","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Probably","significato":"to sulk, pout","termine_origine":"*būd-","catena":[{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*būd-","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*beu-","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Inherited from Middle French bouder, from Old French bouder (“to sulk”, literally “to swell or protrude the lip”), from a root *bod- (“to swell”) (compare Walloon boder (“to swell”)), probably from Proto-Germanic *būd-, *beud-, *buzda-, *bus- (“to swell”), from Proto-Indo-European *beu-, *bu-, *bʰew"},{"parola":"braque","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"pointer (dog breed)","termine_origine":"*brakko","catena":[{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*brakko","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gem-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Proto-Germanic *brakko (“setter”)."},{"parola":"crône","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":2,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"a kind of crane in ports","termine_origine":"*kranô","catena":[{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*kranô","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"en","nome":"English","termine":"crane","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"nl","nome":"Dutch","termine":"kraan","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"nl","ambiti":["mare"],"via":"","testo":"Ultimately in all likelihood from Proto-Germanic *kranô. Said to be from English crane, though the phonetic form might point more to Dutch kraan."},{"parola":"flamberge","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"sword, brand","termine_origine":"*berganą","catena":[{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*berganą","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*bʰergʰ-","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"(1180) From Old French froberge (\"name of a sword\") changed to \"flamberge\" with influence of flambe from Germanic *frōberga composed of the elements *frô (“man”) and bergan (“to protect”) from Proto-Germanic *berganą from Proto-Indo-European *bʰergʰ- (“to take care of, protect, preserve”)"},{"parola":"flotte","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"fleet","termine_origine":"*flutô","catena":[{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*flutô","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gem-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"nrf|frk","testo":"First attested in Old French as flote, from Proto-Germanic *flutô (“a float; raft; boat; ship”) through Norman or Frankish *flote"},{"parola":"fourreau","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"scabbard, sheath","termine_origine":"*fōdrą","catena":[{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*fōdrą","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gem-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Old French furrer, forrel, from fuerre, from Proto-Germanic *fōdrą, though it is not known via which specific Germanic language."},{"parola":"godiche","pos":"adj","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"clumsy, gawky","termine_origine":"*gudą","catena":[{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*gudą","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gem-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Godon, a French surname (from Proto-Germanic *gudą), + -iche."},{"parola":"gravoir","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"graver, burin","termine_origine":"*grabaną","catena":[{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*grabaną","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gem-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From graver + -oir. From Proto-Germanic *grabaną."},{"parola":"hanche","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"hip","termine_origine":"*hanka","catena":[{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*hanka","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gem-pro","ambiti":["scienza"],"via":"","testo":"From Old French, from Proto-Germanic *hanka. Replaced Latin coxa (“hip”), which was retained in French as cuisse (“thigh”). Compare English haunch."},{"parola":"robe","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"dress, frock","termine_origine":"*raubō","catena":[{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*raubō","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gem-pro","ambiti":["moda"],"via":"","testo":"Inherited from Old French, from Proto-Germanic *raubō (“booty”), later \"stolen clothing\"."},{"parola":"soigneur","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"soigneur","termine_origine":"*sunjō","catena":[{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*sunjō","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*h₁sónts","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":["sport"],"via":"","testo":"From soigner (“to look after, take care of; to nurse, treat”) + -eur (suffix forming masculine agent nouns from verbs). Soigner is derived from soin (“care”, noun) (ultimately from Proto-Germanic *sunjō, *sunþijō (“care, responsibility; sooth, truth”), from *sunjaz (“real, true”), from Proto-Indo-Eu"},{"parola":"équiper","pos":"verb","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"to supply","termine_origine":"*skipōną","catena":[{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*skipōną","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gem-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Inherited from Middle French esquiper, from Old French esquiper, eschiper (“to board a ship, set sail”), partly from Old English sċipian (“to board a ship, set sail”) and partly from Old Norse skipa (“to arrange, prepare a ship, equip”); both from Proto-Germanic *skipōną (“to ship, sail, embark”), f"}]}